venue per employee of $1.8M ranks in the top quartile among Healthcare peers, with revenue growing 109%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $232K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $125K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Eton Pharmaceuticals, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $1.8B market cap on $80M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +56% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +323.1pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at -25% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 60% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $10M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 13 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.4\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin -0.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 4.8% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 659% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":6.586243458379809},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 9.5% of float"